AviSynthInternalFilters

Focus implementation derived from AviSynthMinus at commit
dff33dd6978a7781a9a3dd751c85f17184880a04 (release/0.2).

Original sources:
  avs_core/filters/focus.cpp
  avs_core/filters/focus.h
  avs_core/filters/intel/focus_sse.cpp
  avs_core/filters/intel/focus_sse.h
  avs_core/filters/intel/focus_avx2.cpp
  avs_core/filters/intel/focus_avx2.h
  avs_core/core/internal.h (numeric and SSE helper excerpts only)

Original copyright: Avisynth v2.5, Copyright 2002 Ben Rudiak-Gould et al.
Additional original attribution comments are retained in the migrated sources.
Source file SHA-256 values are recorded in source-manifest.json.

The C facade, SDK-independent target organization, plugin assembly and new tests
are migration additions. Behavioral adjustments are recorded in docs/MIGRATION.md.
Production SIMD now uses the vendored Google Highway 1.4.0 source subset.
Highway is separately licensed under Apache-2.0 or BSD-3-Clause; see
third_party/highway/LICENSE and README.avs.md. Its fixed upstream commit and
imported file hashes are recorded in third_party/highway-manifest.json.
The old Focus intrinsics have been removed following migration validation.

The GPL-2.0-or-later license and inherited AviSynth linking exception are retained.
The exception keeps its original wording and scope; the new C interface does not
extend the exception. See LICENSE and the original file headers.

Rotation adapter and scalar YUY2 rotation derived from AviSynthMinus
avs_core/filters/turn.cpp, turn.h and transform.cpp/transform.h at commit
008bf727b6047b8b42e06a84219b45c3ad29e477. Turn code retains Ernst Peche's attribution.
The rotation kernel replaces the old SSE2/SSSE3 turns with Highway and retains
scalar paths for RGB24/48 and YUY2. See original source headers for licensing.
